From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:33:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] leave a decoder's output as the decoder wrote it

A buffer used with the hardware video decoder was taken for a buffer the
host writes, so every CPU mapping for reading transferred the host copy
over the guest pages. The Darwin decoder writes the guest pages of a
classic resource and never its host storage, so the transfer replaced the
decoded picture with whatever the host copy held: a client that read the
output into byte buffers saw stale pictures, and an ImageReader reader
saw the same.

The decoder flag no longer makes a mapping transfer from the host. A
buffer that is also rendered into, or that the camera writes, still does.
---
 virtgpu_virgl.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/virtgpu_virgl.c b/virtgpu_virgl.c
index b018d51596531dd8dafee9ebd4081e61d2bb8486..c2a9ca8d325aaf43640a0d9de8fb24bbe08102b4 100644
--- a/virtgpu_virgl.c
+++ b/virtgpu_virgl.c
@@ -1338,11 +1338,12 @@ static int virgl_bo_invalidate(struct bo *bo, struct mapping *mapping)
 	// Invalidate is only necessary if the host writes to the buffer. The encoder and
 	// decoder flags don't differentiate between input and output buffers, but we can
 	// use the format to determine whether this buffer could be encoder/decoder output.
+	// A decoder writes the guest pages of its output buffer and never the host copy, so
+	// a transfer from the host would replace the decoded picture with stale contents,
+	// and the decoder flag is not a host write.
 	host_write_flags = BO_USE_RENDERING | BO_USE_CAMERA_WRITE | BO_USE_GPU_DATA_BUFFER;
 	if (bo->meta.format == DRM_FORMAT_R8)
 		host_write_flags |= BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER;
-	else
-		host_write_flags |= BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER;
 
 	// TODO(b/267892346): Revert this workaround after migrating to virtgpu_cross_domain
 	// backend since it's a special arc only behavior.
